  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The requirement text is: \"Before that commit, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to check that the book holds exactly the agreed text.\" It does not prescribe a library, algorithm, signature, type, field, or delegation through a named interface. It only says what the skill document must tell agents to do. Any wording, placement, or factoring of that instruction in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` (for example, in the `Workflow` section or in a separate checklist step) would satisfy it equally, as long as it directs the check. The only clause, \"MUST direct agents to check that the book holds exactly the agreed text\", is therefore observable content, not a structural choice. No structural obligation needs implementation evidence, so no `{impl}` marker is required on `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`. Whether the skill's wording actually directs the check is a behavioral and content question for the other criteria.\n\nbehavioral: The subject has one obligation. Before the commit of the agreed requirements, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to check that the book holds exactly the agreed text. `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.commit` supplies the commit context.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_checks_the_book_holds_exactly_the_agreed_text]` is marked `{test}` for the subject. It calls `assert_phrases(\"habeas-requirements\", ...)`, which runs `assert_text` on `bundled_skill(\"habeas-requirements\")`. That text is the skill's `SKILL.md` and reference files, with whitespace collapsed. The assertion requires the phrase \"Check with `git diff` that the book holds exactly the agreed text, then commit it\". If the skill dropped the check, or changed what it checks, the test would fail.\n\nThe phrase contains both the check and \"then commit it\", so the check is directed to come before the commit. The requirement is about skill content, so this text assertion is the observable behavior to test. No other input class or boundary affects the obligation.",
